To solve this system of equations in MATLAB, you can use the `solve` function as you mentioned. Here's the updated code with comments explaining each step:

```matlab
% Define symbols for variables
syms a b c p q r x

% Define equation 1
eq1 = ap + bq + cr == 28;

% Define equation 2
eq2 = a + b + c == 10;

% Define equation 3 (using the given relationship)
eq3 = x == a + 2 * b - c / 3;

% Solve the system of equations for a, b, and c
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], [a, b, c]);

% Extract the values of a, b, and c from the solution
[a_value, b_value, c_value] = sol;

% Calculate the value of x using the relationship in equation 3
x_value = a_value + 2 * b_value - c_value / 3;

% Display the results
disp(['The value of x is: ', num2str(x_value)]);
```

This code will output the value of `x` based on the given system of equations and the relationship provided.

