To identify the tense of a given sentence, you can use natural language processing (NLP) techniques in MATLAB. One approach is to use a pre-trained language model such as BERT or GPT to classify the tense of the sentence. Here's an example using the BERT model from Hugging Face Transformers library:

1. Install the Hugging Face Transformers library in MATLAB by running the following command:
```matlab
!pip install transformers
```
2. Load the BERT model and tokenizer:
```matlab
bert_model = bert('bert-base-uncased');
bert_tokenizer = bert_model.tokenizer;
```
3. Define a function to tokenize and classify the tense of a sentence:
```matlab
function tense = identify_tense(sentence)
    % Tokenize the sentence
    tokens = bert_tokenizer(sentence);

    % Classify the tense using the BERT model
    outputs = bert_model(tokens);
    probabilities = softmax(outputs);
    max_probability = max(probabilities(:));
    tense = bert_tokenizer.convert_ids_to_tokens(argmax(probabilities(:)));
end
```
4. Test the function with the given sentence:
```matlab
sentence = 'I would like to have a meeting today';
tense = identify_tense(sentence);
disp(['The tense of the sentence is: ', tense]);
```
