To design methods to open and close the camera and microphone in JavaScript, you'll need to use the `navigator.mediaDevices` API. Here are four methods that can help you achieve this:

1. Open Camera:

```javascript
async function openCamera() {
  const stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ video: true });
  return stream;
}
```

2. Close Camera:

```javascript
function closeCamera(stream) {
  if (stream) {
    stream.getTracks().forEach((track) => track.stop());
  }
}
```

3. Open Microphone:

```javascript
async function openMicrophone() {
  const stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: true });
  return stream;
}
```

4. Close Microphone:

```javascript
function closeMicrophone(stream) {
  if (stream) {
    stream.getTracks().forEach((track) => track.stop());
  }
}
```

To use these methods, you can call them like this:

