To prevent your generated planets from being too close together, you can introduce a minimum distance between them during the generation process. You can achieve this by modifying your `generateRandomPlanets` function like so:

```javascript
const generateRandomPlanets = (numPlanets, minDistance) => {
  const planets = [];
  let attempts = 0;

  while (planets.length < numPlanets && attempts < 100) {
    attempts++;

    const planet = {
      position: [
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
      ],
      size: randomSize(1, 5) * scale,
      color: randomColor(),
      ringSize: 0.2 * scale,
      ringColor: randomColor(),
      ringNoise: 0.3 * scale,
    };

    // Check if planet is too close to any existing planet
    const tooClose = planets.some((p) =>
      p.position.some((coord, index) => {
        return Math.abs(coord - planet.position[index]) < minDistance
      })
    );

    if (!tooClose) {
      planets.push(planet);
    }
  }

  return planets;
};
```

In this modified version, we added a `minDistance` parameter to the function, which specifies the minimum distance between two planets. Inside the loop, we check if the newly generated planet is too close to any existing planet using the `tooClose` variable. If it's not too close, we add it to the `planets` array.

To use this modified function, simply call it with the desired number of planets and minimum distance, like this:

```javascript
const planets = generateRandomPlanets(5, 35);
```

This will ensure that the generated planets are spaced apart at least `minDistance` units away from each other. Adjust the `minDistance` value to control the density of your planets.

Here's a simple React utility to remove widows. This component will check if there are any words that are too long and break them into smaller ones to avoid widows.

```javascript
import React, { useRef } from 'react';

const RemoveWidows = ({ text }) => {
  const textRef = useRef(null);

  const handleTextChange = () => {
    const text = textRef.current.value;
    const words = text.split(' ');
    const maxWidth = 100; // Adjust this value based on your desired maximum width

    const newText = words.map((word) => {
      if (word.length > maxWidth) {
        return word.slice(0, maxWidth) + '\n';
      }
      return word;
    }).join(' ');

    textRef.current.value = newText;
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <textarea ref={textRef} value={text} onChange={handleTextChange} />
    </div>
  );
};

export default RemoveWidows;
```

To use this component, simply import it and pass in the text you want to check for widows:

```javascript
import RemoveWidows from './RemoveWidows';

const App = () => {
  const text = 'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed non risus. Suspendisse lectus tortor, dignissim sit amet, adipiscing nec, ultricies sed, dolor. Cras mattis consectetur purus, sed tincidunt magna aliquet non.';

  return (
    <div>
      <RemoveWidows text={text} />
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;
```

To update your application without replacing the existing EXE, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a new folder in a temporary location to extract the ZIP file.
2. Extract the contents of the ZIP file into the temporary folder.
3. Copy the updated DLLs and other necessary files from the temporary folder to the application's directory.
4. Update the application's configuration file (e.g., app.config or web.config) with any necessary changes.
5. Restart the application to apply the updates.

Here's some sample code to demonstrate this process:
```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Threading;

namespace ApplicationUpdater
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string tempFolder = Path.GetTempFileName();
            Directory.CreateDirectory(tempFolder);

            string zipFile = "your_zip_file.zip";
            string applicationDirectory = "your_application_directory";

            // Extract the ZIP file
            ZipFile.ExtractToDirectory(zipFile, tempFolder);

            // Copy the updated files to the application directory
            foreach (string file in Directory.GetFiles(tempFolder))
            {
                string destinationFile = Path.Combine(applicationDirectory, Path.GetFileName(file));
                File.Copy(file, destinationFile, true);
            }

            // Update the application's configuration file
            string configFile = "your_configuration_file.config";
            if (File.Exists(Path.Combine(applicationDirectory, configFile)))
            {
                string updatedConfigFile = Path.Combine(tempFolder, configFile);
                File.Copy(updatedConfigFile, Path.Combine(applicationDirectory, configFile), true);
            }

            // Restart the application
            Process.Start(applicationDirectory, "/restart");

            // Clean up the temporary folder
            Directory.Delete(tempFolder, true);
        }
    }
}
```
Replace `"your_zip_file.zip"` with the path to your ZIP file and `"your_application_directory"` with the path to your application directory.

